  "subtitle": "A two-handed keyboard where every stroke types an entire syllable — press several keys at once and the machine spells the sound",
  "why_scout_cares": "The museum has several one-hand chording keyboards but nothing that types whole syllables per stroke with a full two-hand interleaved layout. The Velotype is orthographic chording at 200 wpm — letters produced by language rules, not shorthand. Weird, commercially real, and unlike every other text-entry device in the collection.",
